course: dictionary
lesson: 2201
title: Many meanings of count
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word count has more than one meaning, so look at the words around it to decide which one fits. In «count "One--two--three!"» it means say numbers in order.
explain: When count means find how many things there are, the sentence usually has things to count. «Counting the seconds between the flash and the bang» means finding out how many seconds there are, and that tells you whether the storm is coming closer.
explain: Count can also mean matter or be allowed, as in «that goal doesn't count». A count is the number you get after you have counted. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
fact: To count is to say numbers in order, like «count to ten».
fact: To count is to find how many things there are, like «count the apples».
fact: To count means to matter or be allowed, like «that goal doesn't count».
fact: To count on someone is to trust them, and a count is the number you get by counting.
fact: In maths, counting on means adding by counting forward, and counting back means subtracting. Skip-counting in twos, fives or tens leads to multiplying.
exercise: The zebra and the giraffe count "One--two--three!" What does count mean here? | Find how many things there are | A number you get by counting | Trust someone | *Say numbers in order
exercise: «Count each kind of coin, multiply by its value, and add all the amounts.» What does count mean here? | *Find how many of each coin there are | Matter or be allowed | Trust someone | Say numbers in order to ten
exercise: «That goal doesn't count.» What does count mean here? | Find how many goals there are | Trust the goal | Say numbers in order | *Matter or be allowed
test: «Money boxes with counters can be wrong, so count yourself now and then.» Which meaning fits? | Trust someone | Say numbers backwards | Matter or be allowed | *Find how many coins there are
test: In maths, «counting on» from 7 by adding 3 gives what answer? | Skip the number 7 | Count back and take away | *Count forward and reach 10 | Count in tens from zero
exam: A count is which of these? | To trust someone | *The number you get after counting | To matter or be allowed | To say numbers in order
